{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s28CustomDebugStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s17CustomReflectableP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/Se","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/SE","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/SQ","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s30ExpressibleByDictionaryLiteralP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/SH","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/adjacencylistmodule\/adjacencylist"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed graph stored as out- and in-adjacency lists."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AdjacencyList","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The vertex set is any set of ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" values. The edge set is a set of ordered pairs of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices: self-loops are allowed, parallel edges are not.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vertices are kept in dense slots, with a dictionary from vertex to slot. Edges are kept in an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array, so an edge’s position in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":" is an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<edgeCount"},{"type":"text","text":", and a weight can live"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in an array beside the graph. Each slot has a row of the slots of its out-neighbors, a parallel"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row of those edges’ positions, and a row of its in-neighbors; the rows of each kind share one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array, so the graph makes a constant number of allocations however many vertices it has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(amortized, like "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Array"},{"type":"text","text":"), and copying it copies a constant number of buffers. A dictionary from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"slot pair to position answers "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains(edge:)"},{"type":"text","text":" in O(1)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Removing an edge is O(1): the last edge moves into its position, and the last entry of each row"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"into the hole. Removing a vertex costs O(degree) and moves the last slot into its place. So"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex order, edge order and edge positions are unspecified and may change after a removal."}]}],"ki